13.11.4. 
What is the purpose of the Program?  
The AI Friday aims to foster innovation and problem-solving through the 
development of AI-powered tools that align with real-world business challenges and 
emerging technology trends. It is an opportunity to showcase talent, creativity, and 
technical expertise. 
13.11.5. 
Who can participate? 
Anyone within TCS with passion to solve problem using AI - from beginners to 
experienced professionals. Basic LLM familiarity is recommended. You may build with 
Python, .NET, Java, or use Langflow for no-code agents.  
13.11.6. 
Do I need prior experience in AI or programming? 
No. You may use Python, .NET, Java, or build solutions in Langflow without 
coding. Basic LLM familiarity is recommended. 
13.11.7. 
What if I do not have experience in Python or GenAI? 
You can connect with Talent Development to upskill yourself. 
13.11.8. 
What kind of projects or activities will we be working on? 
Projects may range from building ML models and using AI APIs to tackling 
real-world problems with data-driven solutions 
13.11.9. 
Is this a team-based or individual event? 
It’s a team event, either you can form your own team and nominate or 
nominate individually (Refer: 6). If nominated individually, organizers will form a 
team using power of AI. 
13.11.10. 
Will resources be provided? 
Yes. Participants will receive Laptop loaded with Python, VS Code, access to 
open Internet, relevant tools, and mentoring support. 
13.11.11. 
What mindset should I have while building my solution for the AI 
Hackathon?  
You should build your solution with an enterprise application development 
mindset, focusing on scalability, reliability, and maintainability.  
13.11.12.  
What tools or platforms will we be using?  
